## 17. Acceptance Criteria

The controlled test passes when:

- One existing equipment instance receives verified live OPC process measurements.
- The original SCADA screens display those measurements without binding changes.
- The FAT-approved hierarchy and UDT structure remain unchanged.
- Existing alarm and status logic remain intact.
- Existing data types and engineering units are preserved.
- No unrelated equipment is affected.
- No unauthorized equipment writes occur.
- Configuration differences are limited to approved data source changes.
- A targeted rollback package is available.

Report separately any acceptance criteria that could not be tested.

Do not characterize this controlled test as completion of formal SAT execution.

## 18. Final Instructions

The existing application is the design authority.

Adapt the OPC mappings to the deployed UDTs. Do not adapt the deployed UDT structure to the OPC mappings.

Prefer configuration changes over architectural changes.

If the proposed integration cannot be implemented without modifying the FAT-approved structure, stop and provide the technical justification and minimum alternative change for review.
